     "<div class=\"gmail_quote\"><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0 0 0 .8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div><a title=\"This question does not show any research effort; it is unclear or not useful\" style=\"text-align:center;margin-right:auto;margin-bottom:10px;margin-left:auto;color:rgb(0,119,204);font-size:1px;overflow:hidden;width:40px;min-height:30px;display:inline!important;background-image:url(&quot;&quot;),none;background-position:0px -220px;background-repeat:no-repeat\" rel=\"nofollow\">n vote</a><br></div><div style=\"text-align:center;min-width:46px\"><a href=\"http://stackoverflow.com/questions/38338438/when-faceting-with-ggplot-and-plotly-the-points-are-plotted-in-the-incorrect-fac#\" title=\"Click to mark as favorite question (click again to undo)\" style=\"margin-right:auto;margin-bottom:2px;margin-left:auto;color:rgb(0,119,204);font-size:1px;overflow:hidden;display:block;width:40px;min-height:30px;background-image:url(&quot;&quot;),none;background-position:0px -120px;background-repeat:no-repeat\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://stackoverflow.com/questions/38338438/when-faceting-with-ggplot-and-plotly-the-points-are-plotted-in-the-incorrect-fac%23&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792367816110000&amp;usg=AOvVaw28wGqpkxpIGPcd_FXS_2Yy\">favorite</a><div><span style=\"color:rgb(106,115,124)\"></span></div></div><div style=\"font-size:15px;width:660px;word-wrap:break-word;line-height:1.3\"><p style=\"margin-bottom:1em;clear:both\">I have a shiny app that plots data that is queried from our company database. You can choose to facet the plot based on different columns in the dataframe. I am using facet_grid and two selectInputs to facet from the side, top or both. I am also building a ggplot object and then using plotly_build to make a plotly plot in shiny. I have tried to solve the problem outside of the shiny app by faceting <code style=\"